# Line endings are normalised to LF in the index *and* the working tree, on
# every platform. This repository had no `.gitattributes` at all, so the only
# thing keeping LF in the index was every contributor happening to have
# `core.autocrlf=true` — an unenforced convention, not a guarantee.
#
# The scripts below are why that matters. A shell script committed with CRLF
# fails on Linux with `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M`, and the two places it would
# surface are the least convenient possible: CI, and `scripts/install.sh`, which
# users run. Nothing is broken today (every script is LF in the index); this is
# what keeps it that way.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Stated explicitly as well as covered by the rule above. These execute on Linux
# and inside containers, where a stray CR is fatal rather than cosmetic, so the
# intent should survive someone narrowing the blanket rule later.
*.sh text eol=lf
ops/bootstrap/*.sh text eol=lf

# Generated by `cargo run -p dpp-evidence --example generate_dataset`. Several
# are deliberately tampered fixtures for the offline verifier, so hand-editing
# one is how you get a fixture that no longer demonstrates what it claims to.
# Collapsed in review; they are data, not code.
ops/demo/dossiers/*.json linguist-generated
